# A head with no fallback: when the condition is false the index fails.
-- source.cue --
n: "a" | "b"
-- target.cue --
s: string
-- lens.cue --
input: _
result: {s: [if input.n == "a" {"x"}][0]}
-- out --
unknown
result.s takes the first element of a list built by if input.n == "a" with no fallback, so when the condition is false the list is empty and the index fails; add a fallback element: [if c {x}, y][0] (rule unknown-head) @ lens.cue:2:13
